This run was the result of some renewed hope of ascending (finally) in
this ridiculous game. After spending an obscene amount of time in the
spoilers, I decided to re-attempt the completion of NetHack.

Sticking with the fairly stereotypical neutral human Valkyrie, I
played to the strength of familiarity. Found an early key, un-IDed bag
and a wand of magic missile, explored/trapdoored through the mainly-
darkened Mines (picking up poison resistance) and wound up at the
town, to discover an imminent lack of general store (woo!), and a
coaligned altar (genuine woo!) to play around with. Picked up some
candles to descend with.

Went to the hardware store and found a towel, as well as an identical
bag to my held one; price-IDed it to be expensive. Tested with stones,
and success: a Dlvl:1 bag of holding!

Meticulously stashed potions and scrolls in the bag while progressing
downward. Picked up a bit of nice armour (namely +1 iron boots, a
blessed dwarvish helm and some dwarvish mithril). Had a nasty
encounter with a rust monster that left my helm and sword worse for
wear; ditched both after finding a + 2 dwarvish helm and a katana.
Found a wand of safety (aka teleportation).

Mimic of the Mines yielded a lovely loadstone, plus a heap of gems
(thank God for spoilers!) and a luckstone. Took the stone up to the
altar, did a water-prayer and ended up getting "a golden glow". BUC-
tested all my stuff, then headed back up to the Dungeons. Explored a
few of the missed dark levels with a brass lamp (which died fairly
quickly).

Hit Dlvl:3 out of the mines, and discovered a nice little armour shop.
At XP:10, decided to relinquish the 'keeper of his humble abode, and
suffered minor injuries in the process. Looted a pair of soccer boots,
a team shirt and a very nice crystal plate mail.

Sailing smoothly, I then made a huge mistake: getting attacked by a
wood nymph and _not_ killing it. The bitch took my shirt, helm, armour
and katana, leaving me with two wands of striking (one empty), and a
pickaxe. Finally killed her, but lost the armour to striking :(

Headed back to the penthouse and retrieved my old dwarvern mithril.
Just about to set out a little further, maybe to make some more holy
water for my luckstone, my bag and my touchstone (once I get it).

